    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13585" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-vĕnĕror</span></b> ,
			ātus, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep. a., to reverence, worship</i>
			(very rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deos prece,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					2, 18</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">somnia ter sanctā deveneranda
					molā,</span>”
				i. e. <i>to avert by prayers</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tib.
					1, 5, 14</span></i>
			.</div>
